  "slug": "high-resolution-5b11",
  "summary": "Nanopore and lesion-mapping methods now read replication, DNA structure and abasic lesions per molecule and per nucleotide in genomic DNA.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is sequencing-based mapping of DNA features at molecular resolution, with computational inference applied to raw or labelled reads. ForkML combines a machine learning method for nanopore reads with multipulse BrdU labelling to map replication forks at single-molecule, kilobase resolution across the human genome. A second preprint detects alternative DNA conformations from Oxford Nanopore long reads after permanganate probing, using logistic regression, random forest, XGBoost and 1D CNN models on raw current data. DEPACE-seq, a published method, maps abasic sites at single-nucleotide resolution and characterises dynamic, long-lived AP landscapes in mammalian genomes. What is new is the shift toward per-molecule and per-nucleotide readouts of replication, DNA structure and lesion states in genomic DNA.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-07-23"
}
